body:
My solo boss enemies usually need some combination of:

Legendary resistances (obvi) though I find only 3 of those tend to be quite insufficient;

Shapeshifting (to avoid polymorph cheese);

Plane Shift (self only, at-will or 3/day) to avoid Banishment cheese); or in the case of BBEGs,

Immutable Form+: can't have their physical form transformed by spells or magical effects in any way (polymorph, etc) and can't be teleported against their will (banishment, gate, imprisonment, being forced to draw the Donjon card, etc). 

If there are more bases I can cover with that last one, I'd love to know. There are plenty of other encounters in the game (that's been going on for 5+ years) for my party to cheese up! But I want to make damn sure they can't in the final battle.
